use "@std"

Note: DEFER-01 (Phase 20-01) — range(Int, Int) two-arg form
Int[] r1 = (range 0 5)
(print (concat "range 0 5 ok len=" (str (len r1))))

Note: DEFER-01 — range(Int, Int, Int) three-arg form, positive step
Int[] r2 = (range 0 10 2)
(print (concat "range 0 10 2 ok len=" (str (len r2))))

Note: DEFER-01 — range(Int, Int, Int) three-arg form, negative step.
Note: 20-RESEARCH Pitfall 4: parser interprets `-1` in arg position as binary
Note: subtraction (collapses to one arg). Bind via `(sub 0 1)` first, mirrors
Note: tests/test_slice.flow:6 convention.
Int negOne = (sub 0 1)
Int[] r3 = (range 5 0 negOne)
(print (concat "range 5 0 -1 ok len=" (str (len r3))))

Note: empty range — start equals end
Int[] r4 = (range 0 0)
(print (concat "range 0 0 empty len=" (str (len r4))))

(print "test_range: PASSED")
